   "id": 9047,
   "options": {
    "content": "### Tensor-parallel ring sharding\n\nTwo Mac minis run **one distributed model**: `mlx.launch` splits every tensor-parallel dimension across both ranks and synchronizes with ring allreduce over the dedicated 10-GbE link (`10.0.0.1` \u2194 `10.0.0.2`).\n\n* **Attention heads** (16 KV-grouped / 32 linear-value) and the **MLP intermediate** (9216) are split ~50/50 across ranks.\n* **KV cache** lives per-rank (its own sequence/key-value storage) \u2014 the KV agent (`mlx_kv_*`) tracks the pooled view.\n* The **ring carries the allreduce traffic**: watch `mlx_net_*` \u2014 at ~75 MB/s during generation it is the pipeline's third busiest resource after the GPU and the KV cache.\n* **Linear attention** (Qwen3.5) reduces KV pressure: 128-d key/value heads with a 4-tap conv, plus 1 **MTP** layer for multi-token prediction.\n\nWeight shard per rank \u2248 `worker_rss / 2` (fp16) plus quantized intermediate buffers; GPU headroom is `mlx_hw_gpu_mem_alloc_bytes` vs `mlx_hw_gpu_mem_total_bytes`.",
    "mode": "markdown"
   },
   "title": "",
   "type": "text"
  }
